    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Interpretation rules",
      "Anchor": "interpretation-rules",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Interpretation rules"
      ],
      "Text": "A workplace record means that employment was verified, not that the member is currently employed. Current and past employment are indistinguishable by design.\nOrder is not meaningful. Do not infer recency or seniority from list order.\nAbsence is not a negative signal. Never treat it as a red flag.\nExpect partial coverage. Data is shared only with member consent and certified partners, so it is present for a subset of applicants.\nverificationMethod only applies to WORKPLACE records; it\u0027s not populated for IDENTITY records.\nverifiedName fields (firstName, middleName, lastName) aren\u0027t guaranteed to all be populated. What\u0027s returned depends on the identity verification vendor, so handle missing name parts gracefully.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
